  {
    "insert": "\n"
  },
  {
    "insert": "Weakness:",
    "attributes": {
      "bold": true
    }
  },
  {
    "insert": "\nThe methodology describes how the individual research questions are answered. Unfortunately, the methodology is completely missing in your exposé. Read through your research questions again carefully and think about which methods you could use to answer them. Also think about the difficulties and limitations that could arise from your methodology."
  },
  {
    "insert": "\n",
    "attributes": {
      "list": "bullet"
    }
  },
  {
    "insert": "The anchor within the motivation should explain to the reader why the chosen topic is relevant and what consequences the problem may have. Your work does not explain the problem sufficiently to convey its relevance. Think again about why the topic is relevant and add the explanation to the text. You should also go into more detail about the current handling/criticism of this problem. "
  },
  {
    "insert": "You should explain the problems in the education system more clearly.",
    "attributes": {
      "background": "#ffffff"
    }
  },
  {
    "insert": "\n",
    "attributes": {
      "list": "bullet"
    }
  },
  {
    "insert": "Within the theoretical framework, the theories used in the work are presented and their relevance justified. Your theoretical framework is somewhat missing. Read through further literature on your topic and see if you can find a precise theory. You should link your theory to your methodology."
  },
  {
    "insert": "\n",
    "attributes": {
      "list": "bullet"
    }
  },
  {
    "insert": "The state of the art should present your work in comparison to existing research. The weaknesses and relevance of your SOTA are mentioned, but should be explained in more detail. Read the section again carefully and add further explanations and details."
  },
  {
    "insert": "\n",
    "attributes": {
      "list": "bullet"
    }
  },
  {
    "insert": "The time schedule is used to plan the thesis in advance to see whether it is possible in the short time available. It is therefore very important that all aspects of the thesis are included. The writing of the thesis is missing in your time schedule. Think about which chapters all belong in a thesis and when they should best be written. Also add more details to your description."
  },
  {
    "insert": "\n",
    "attributes": {
      "list": "bullet"
    }
  },
  {
    "insert": "A well-organised exposé is crucial for clarity and readability. A consistent structure helps to guide the reader smoothly through the content, making complex ideas easier to follow and understand. The structure and reading flow in your work can still be improved. Read through your exposé carefully and try to connect the individual aspects and parts. "
  },
  {
    "insert": "\n",
    "attributes": {
      "list": "bullet"
    }
  },
  {
    "insert": "In scientific work it is very important to have a standardised terminology. Abbreviations must always be introduced at the beginning (e.g. ‘AI’) and then used consistently (e.g. ‘LLM’). Unfortunately, you have not achieved this in your text. Go through your text again carefully and adjust the abbreviations."
  },
  {
    "insert": "\n",
    "attributes": {
      "list": "bullet"
    }
  },
  {
    "insert": "In scientific papers, it is very important to avoid errors in spelling and grammar. Your work contains some spelling mistakes (e.g. \"feedbacks\" - \"feedback\"; \"conserns\" - \"concerns\") and grammatical errors. In addition, many sentences could be formulated more scientifically and indirectly (e.g. \""
  },
  {
    "insert": "Large Language Models (LLMs) are becoming increasingly prominent.\")",
